Both.  C-sets get very short shrift in CLL, a mere mention of lV'e in the g=
adri section and little else expository, even in MEX.  And no uses them in =
the language, partly because of the CLL situation and partly because of the=
 belief that they are virtually uselss (i.e., can only be used as in set th=
eory).  As for useful places to look for information about L-sets, the vari=
ous things Google supplies (under Lesniewski and mereology) tend to be rath=
er technical and wrapped up in the particularities of the system (and relat=
ed systems) rather than the matters of interest to Lojban.  You can eventua=
lly work out the good stuff but it is a bit uphill.  I can't find a popular=
 or directed discussion anywhere -- of L-sets or related notions.  =20


